# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit. `.env.example` IS committed -- it holds key *prefixes*
# for validation, no live values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*credential*
*secret*
real/freellm/config.json
real/freellm/gateway.env
real/freellm/gateway.env.bak
real/freellm/unified.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Manuscript. Source is tracked so the arXiv build is reproducible from this
# repository; LaTeX intermediates and generated files are not. `main.tex` and
# `main-8pp.tex` are OUTPUTS of render.py -- editing them is a mistake the
# build warns about, so they are deliberately untracked and the .tmpl files
# are the authored source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
paper/main.tex
paper/main-8pp.tex
paper/*.aux
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.toc
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.omc/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
paper/*.bak-*
paper/*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# realness/ additions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Episode checkouts are regenerated by the runner and are large. The append-only
# episode log and the analysis artifacts under results/exp0/ ARE tracked -- the
# paper reads only from results/.
results/exp0/checkouts/
results/exp0/replay/
results/exp1/checkouts/
results/exp1/surface_check/
results/exp1-selftest/

# Activation cache: 410 MB, deterministic in (model, dtype, stimuli), regenerated in ~3.5 min.
# The verdict it feeds IS tracked, in results/exp0/exp0.json.
results/exp0/activations-*.npz

# The manuscript is GENERATED by paper/render.py from main.tex.tmpl. Editing main.tex directly is
# a mistake, so it is untracked; the .tmpl is the authored source.
paper/main.tex
paper/*.aux
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.pdf

# Run logs ARE tracked. They were previously excluded as transient console output, on the
# reasoning that only the structured artifacts are evidence. That reasoning was wrong for an
# artifact meant to be audited: the logs are the only record of what a run actually did as it did
# it -- when an arm completed, whether a supervisor intervened, which cells were retried, how long
# a GPU stage took. A reader checking whether a reported number came from the run it claims to
# cannot get that from the verdict JSON alone.
#
# What stays excluded is only output that is bulky AND deterministically regenerable from what is
# tracked: episode checkouts, replay trees, and the activation cache.

# The slide PDF is a build product of docs/index.html, regenerated by
# scripts/export_slides_pdf.py. The HTML deck is the tracked source.
docs/*.pdf
